From 583d9158342a14fd29638919493462753428234a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cpkt9762 <cpkt9762@163.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 03:49:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(plugin): Paseo adapter for cloud sync and memory
 browsing

Add plugin/paseo, a TypeScript plugin for the Paseo desktop and mobile
app. It does not register an engram MCP, so the Claude, Codex, Pi and DSH
integrations keep their own tools; it only adds what Paseo can show:

- A header button in every workspace. Unenrolled projects get "join sync",
  which scans the project's prompts for credential-looking text, lets the
  user delete matches one by one, and then enrolls (or enrolls anyway on
  an explicit choice). Enrolled projects show a menu with stop sync, open
  memory and view status. The state machine treats a timed-out write as
  "outcome unknown" and re-reads the real state instead of retrying.
- A sidebar footer row and a status screen showing the sync status of the
  selected host: red for lost auth, a policy denial of a named project,
  degraded or repeated failures, yellow for retained dead rows, paused,
  backoff, stale status or an old backlog, gray when unsupported.
- A workspace panel that searches and lists the project's memories and
  prompts. Prompts always come from the masked projection, and deletes are
  bound to the engram instance and the project.

The client only talks to a loopback engram over HTTP, refuses redirects,
times out after five seconds, never retries writes, probes the sync-admin
capability instead of guessing from 404, and never exposes the optional
ENGRAM_HTTP_TOKEN to the app. It uses no runtime dependency beyond what
Paseo provides (the SDK, zod, react and react-native) and does not import
outside its own directory. Workspace lists use the protocol's 200 page
limit and never ask for background workspaces, which hosts must opt into.

Requires Paseo 0.13 or newer (checked against 0.14.0) and an engram that
reports sync-admin-v2. Install with
`paseo plugin install <dir> --home <daemon home>`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
